 ## 📈 Dashboard Visualizations

 ### 🏦 1. Loan Type Interest

 The **Loan Type Interest** chart compares interest values across different loan categories.

```
Home        ███████████████████████
Education   █████████████████████
Car         ███████████
Business    █████████████████
```

 This visualization helps users understand how interest is distributed among different loan types.

---

 ### 💼 2. Employment Status Analysis

 The employment-status visualization breaks down the dataset according to different employment/education categories.

 📊 It can be used to examine relationships between:

```
👤 Customer
   │
   ├── 💼 Employment Status
   ├── 🎓 Education
   ├── 👨 Male / 👩 Female
   └── 💰 Financial Activity
```

 This makes it easier to identify differences in the financial profile of various customer groups.

---

 ### 💳 3. User-wise Monthly EMI

 The **User ID Wise Monthly EMI** visualization shows the distribution of monthly EMI amounts across users.

```
💰 Monthly EMI
     │
     ├── 👤 User 1
     ├── 👤 User 2
     ├── 👤 User 3
     ├── 👤 User 4
     └── ... many users
```

 The pie/donut-style visualization provides a visual representation of how EMI values are distributed.

---

 ### 📊 4. Loan Type Interest Rate

 The **Loan Type Interest Rate** chart compares interest rates across loan categories.

```
🏦 Loan Categories
       │
       ├── 🏠 Home
       ├── 🎓 Education
       ├── 🚗 Car
       └── 🏢 Business
```

 This allows users to visually compare the interest-rate contribution of different types of loans.

---

 ### 📉 5. Financial Distribution Analysis

 The dashboard also includes a detailed chart showing financial values across categories, making it possible to identify:

 - 🔎 High-value categories
- 📉 Lower-value categories
- 📊 Differences between loan types
- 💰 Financial distribution patterns
- 👥 Customer-related trends

